title: Fs::LibSSH bypasses sudo
updated: 2026-08-13T05:01:58Z
---

Fs::LibSSH::_run hardcodes Rex::Interface::Exec->create(LibSSH) instead of letting create() resolve the type from get_connection_type. Connection::LibSSH::get_connection_type returns Sudo under Rex::is_sudo(), so Rex routes to Rex::Interface::Fs::Sudo -- but any Fs operation reached from inside our own class never gets sudo-wrapped.

Decide: document as a limitation, or route through the resolving form (which changes behaviour for every existing caller). Not a drive-by fix.
